### Prose Cards
<hr class="section-rule lvl-3">

The `.cmk-card` blockquote (see `docs/cmk/index`) turns any blockquote into a
frosted editorial card: a Frost left-accent, an enlarged initial, a Frost-tinted
bold lead-in as the title, and quiet italics.  It is opt-in, page-independent, and
refinable; all in pure Markdown via `attr_list`, with no macro or page-class.

#### Default Card
<hr class="section-rule lvl-4">

A blockquote whose lead paragraph is tagged `{: .cmk-card }`:

```markdown
> **Tier-1 Roots.**  CMK is a *strict superset* of Makefile, which is
> itself basically a superset of bash.
> {: .cmk-card }
```

> **Tier-1 Roots.**  CMK is a *strict superset* of Makefile, which is itself basically a superset of bash.  It's the ground floor for the everyday dirty work of adhoc-automation, with zero friction in the middle.  Foundational, no-ceremony stuff here, but you can start structured and stay structured with a clear promotion path.
> {: .cmk-card }

<hr style="width:95%;border-bottom:1px dashed black;">

A default card can also wrap a collapsed demo embed (as on the CMK landing page):

> **With an Embedded Demo.**  The card's frosted panel wraps a nested collapsed demo, so prose and source read as one unit.
> {: .cmk-card }
>
{{ ('> ' ~ site.embed_demo('demos/cmk/tier-1.cmk', github=github, collapsed=True)) | replace('\n', '\n> ') }}

