#### Refined Cards (Custom Class)
<hr class="section-rule lvl-4">

Refine a card by passing a second class alongside `.cmk-card`.  Each modifier keys
off the lead paragraph's extra class, no macro, no page-class:

```markdown
> **Aurora Accent.**  prose ...
> {: .cmk-card .card-aurora }
```

`.card-aurora`: swaps the Frost accent, initial, and title for an Aurora-red one:

> **Aurora Accent.**  This card opts into the Aurora-red accent by passing `.card-aurora` as a custom class beside `.cmk-card`.  *The initial, border, and title-color all follow the accent.*
> {: .cmk-card .card-aurora }

<!-- card-break: prevents python-markdown from merging adjacent blockquotes -->

`.card-tight`: trims the padding and margins for a denser card:

> **Tight Card.**  This card passes `.card-tight` to compress its padding and margins, useful for a run of stacked cards.
> {: .cmk-card .card-tight }

<!-- card-break: prevents python-markdown from merging adjacent blockquotes -->

`.card-plain`: drops the frosted panel, backdrop-blur, and shadow, keeping only the accent + editorial signature:

> **Plain Card.**  This card passes `.card-plain` to shed the frosted panel and shadow, leaving just the Frost accent rule and the enlarged initial.
> {: .cmk-card .card-plain }

